con__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merinoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/902755-alternate-ancient-sumerian-character-creation#post902755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to recall there being some sort of alternate character creation for Forsaken that involved an ancient world setting and made them quite a bit stronger? I may be remembering this completely wrong but it may have been in a Dark Eras setting or published on one of the writer's blogs? Anybody recall this or know where I can find it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Forsaken Chronicler's Guide (I want to say part 3?) has a Hunting Ground for Ancient Sumer, where the Forsaken are revered as the Ur-Sag in the city-state of Bau. It's great stuff.<br /> <br /> Attributes are 7/6/5, Skills are 20/16/10, 12 Merit dots, 10 dits of Gifts, 10 dots of Renown, Primal Urge 3, +3 on rolls to resist Kuruth, add their highest Renown as a social bonus when dealing with mortals and their lowest tl dealing with spirits, and they can remain in Gauru indefinitely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T14:20:58-07:00","id":903002,"title":"","content":"That's it! Thanks a ton guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1007-merinoc","name":"Merinoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T14:29:35-07:00","id":903010,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting the benefits are from a massive fetish, and the spirits were essentially dicking them around the whole time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T14:53:03-07:00","id":903028,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see/do a rewrite of that setting now that we know how relatively recent the Sundering was, and make it pre/during the Oaths of the Moon Era, and have the Dog-Kings be the last hurrah of trying to forge a new purpose for themselves before its colossal failure and the &quot;return to Luna and the Hunt&quot; factions win out and become the Tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourwea